From 8349b443344195c169340100d042a4e38735ef38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:37:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the conversion under the GUI raised one level
 at a time where its frames do not keep up

CDVGuiLevel takes the place of CDVGuiRound: every frame is drawn at level 0,
the conversion as 9ff2bad had it, and the frames with GUI elements of a profile
5 picture go up one level only where they are measured not to keep up at their
level, by the same rule (GPU time over the mark of CDVStepDown and missed
refreshes, two windows in a row or one beyond the period, nothing while frames
can still be presented a frame ahead, nothing in the seconds after a seek or
after GUI elements come), up to the highest the bridge can draw: level 1 (the
same bytes) first, level 2 (the simplified rounding) only where level 1 does
not keep up either. Each level comes down by one when the level below would
take, by the ratio measured when it went up, no more than the release mark,
after a minute of film at it; where it has to go up again before the level
below kept up for a minute, its wait doubles. Frames without GUI elements, a
GPU that keeps up and the frames of profile 7 FEL and 8.1 stay at level 0.

The targets of levels 1 and 2 are freed when the last format above level 0
comes down to it, and when native output ends. The GPU time of a frame is
taken with the pace it was presented at, not the pace when its time is read.
A log line for each change (level 2, as before: "the rounding of the
conversion under the GUI is simplified (at most 1 code in near-ties)"), and
the player information says so while frames are drawn at level 2.

The decision has a host test (both ways, the levels, 71 checks) and 21
mutations of it, all caught.
